# Wire Format Rules

## Encoding

- All integers little-endian
- No padding, no alignment
- No `usize` — only fixed-width types
- Use `to_le_bytes()` / `from_le_bytes()` exclusively

## Decoding Safety

- Bounds-check before every slice access
- Check resource limits before every allocation
- Return `Error::UnexpectedEof` on truncation
- Return `Error::ResourceLimitExceeded` on oversized claims
- Never trust payload_len without checking against buffer remaining

## Format Reference

Refer to PLAN.md "Wire Format v2" section for the canonical spec:
- Header: 6 bytes (magic ATSC + version + flags)
- Frame: 9 + payload_len bytes (codec_id + sample_count + payload_len + payload)
- Footer: 8 bytes (magic CSTA + frame_count)
